WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.150
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:07.860
I'm in the new LINK VRAINS!

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.840
Looks like a fun city.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:17.340
But what's most surprising is that 
Playmaker has a bounty on his head.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.430
Who are you?

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.140
Stop it!

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.210
Sorry, Playmaker.  I came back.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.480
What will you do next?

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.090
Challenge him to a duel.

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:42.050
In the new LINK VRAINS' duel 
rules, winners can make trades.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:45.300
If I defeat him in a 
duel, I can get his data.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.270
I activate one Link Spell from my deck!

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.920
Link Spell?

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.500
I never heard of that!

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:57.400
Battle!  Flow Hydradrive 
attacks you directly!

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.240
Look.  We found your friend.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.220
Friend?  That’s unthinkable.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.960
Don’t associate me with that airhead.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:41.270
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:48.080
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:55.390
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:01.960
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:08.700
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:15.940
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:22.650
I want to share your pain

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:05.500
The other Flow Hydradrive 
attacks you directly!

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.760
This is bad, Playmaker!

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.870
We're already in a huge pinch!

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.970
Linkuriboh’s effect activates!

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.980
When your monster attacks...

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:23.530
...I can tribute this card to lower its 
ATK to 0 until the end of the turn!

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:30.920
Since there's no longer a monster next to 
its link, Elphase’s ATK return to normal.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.670
I end my turn.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.090
You saved us, Linkuriboh!

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:46.140
I always knew you had skill!

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:48.620
See ya!

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.610
Who are you?

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.730
Cyberse-Type and a spell 
card with Link Markers...

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:58.340
Why do you have those?

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.260
Hello?

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.230
We’ll have to catch and question him.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.400
They’re leaving us behind!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.590
Go faster!

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:12.500
Boss, I can't go any faster!

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.300
I can't give more!

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.780
Stop complaining!

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:19.130
Playmaker's D-Board is the newest model!

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:23.650
Make my avatar the newest model too!

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.650
Link Spell and a new enemy...

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.380
What's happening?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.970
Playmaker…

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.580
I don’t know what that 
shiny guy'll do next.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.570
So let’s defeat him quickly.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:47.900
You’re right.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.680
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:56.140
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, One-Time Passcode!

00:04:56.140 --> 00:05:01.080
I Special Summon a Security 
Token in defense position.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.440
Elphase’s effect!

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:09.480
It gains 300 ATK for every 
monster next to its link!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.730
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:15.730
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:20.070
I set Elphase and Security 
Token in the Link Markers!

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.170
Link Summon!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:28.640
Appear, Link 2 Cyberse Witch!

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.620
When the Link Summoned 
Elphase leaves the field...

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:38.180
...I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower Cyberse from my graveyard.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:41.390
Resurrect, Defcon Bird!

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.130
Cyberse Witch’s effect!

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:50.820
Once per turn, when a monster is 
Special Summoned next to its link...

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:56.610
...I banish a spell card from my graveyard 
to add two cards in my deck to my hand!

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:59.340
I banish One-Time Passcode!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:03.080
And when this effect is used, 
once during that turn...

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:08.000
...I can Special Summon a Level 4 
or lower Cyberse from my graveyard!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.010
I Special Summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.060
Du-Du-Duel!

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:25.840
From my hand, I activate the 
Ritual Spell, Cynet Ritual!

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.170
A Ritual Spell?

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:35.020
I tribute monsters from my hand and field 
whose total Level equals or surpasses...

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:40.700
...the Cyberse Ritual Monster that 
I'm Ritual Summoning from my hand!

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:48.090
I tribute Level 4 Cyberse Wizard 
and Level 3 Defcon Bird!

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.610
The contract has been made.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:59.300
The sage who wields dark power 
inherits these two souls!

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.200
Ritual Summon!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:07.000
Rise, Cyberse Magician!

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.180
A Cyberse Ritual Monster?

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.600
That wasn’t in the data!

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.170
I set one card.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:21.240
Cyberse Magician attacks Flow Hydradrive!

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:29.660
When Cyberse Magician battles a 
Link Monster, it gains 1000 ATK!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.000
Not good!  If he takes Cyberse 
Magician’s attack, it’s over!

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.530
Do something!

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:41.690
The Link Spell, Judgment Arrows’ effect!

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:48.980
When the Link Monster linked to 
this card battles, its ATK double!

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:53.220
We have 3500 ATK!

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.220
That’s not enough to stop it!

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:58.910
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Property Spray!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:06.950
Once during each of our turns, I can tribute 
my monster to gain LP equal to its ATK.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.910
I tribute Flow Hydradrive, 
which has 1000 ATK!

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.770
Until the end of this turn...

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:22.750
...your monsters' Attribute becomes the 
same as the tributed monster's - Wind.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.420
A card that changes Attribute.

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:27.740
That doesn’t matter!

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.990
Go, Playmaker!

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.000
Take this!

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.330
Cyberse Magic!

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.940
Nice!

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:49.460
You couldn’t finish him, 
but you dealt big damage!

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:02.140
So that’s his true identity!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.030
Who are you?

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:08.440
I’m…!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.800
I’m…

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.810
Who am I?

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.660
Who am I?

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.980
That’s what we’re supposed to say!

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:31.670
Why are you challenging me to a battle?

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.580
Stop playing dumb!

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:40.230
We’re fighting to beat the bad guy who 
kidnapped our acquaintance's brother!

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.230
What?  Who would do such a horrible thing?

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.200
You!

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:50.470
Me?  I don’t remember doing that!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.670
You forgot what you did?

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:57.430
Did the damage give him amnesia?

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.680
Why am I here?

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:02.930
Big brother!

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.220
Stop wasting time!

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:07.420
Hurry up and chase them away!

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.140
That voice…

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:12.070
Haru!  Your younger brother Haru!

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.430
Younger brother?

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:15.500
Yes, Bohman.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:20.610
You promised that you'd regain our memories!

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.380
That’s right.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.030
My name is Bohman.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:30.240
Our memories are on the line in this duel!

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.210
Memories?

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.660
I can’t afford to lose this duel!

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:38.820
Let’s continue!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.540
Checking duel status.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:45.030
I have 900 LP.  Playmaker has 2000.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.890
Resume the duel!

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.530
Umm, Mr. Bohman?

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.770
Flow Hydradrive’s effect activates!

00:10:53.770 --> 00:11:01.380
When it's destroyed, I Special Summon a 
Hydradrive Token on my field in defense position!

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:08.050
Next, I activate the Continuous Trap, 
Hydradrive Generator’s effect!

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:13.650
When I summon or Special Summon 
when I have fewer LP than you...

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:20.330
...I Special Summon a Hydradrive Token 
in defense position once per turn!

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.560
What’s up with this guy?

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.580
So he's decided to duel?

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:29.070
Ai has no clue what he really wants to do.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:33.070
For now, our priority is 
to take back what he stole.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:38.240
Cyberse Witch attacks Hydradrive Token!

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:43.810
I end my turn.

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:49.490
Cyberse Magician and Cyberse Witch’s 
Attributes change back to normal.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:52.650
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.970
Appear!  The circuit that connects the truth!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.770
The summoning condition is one Hydradrive!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.410
Link Summon!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:07.910
Link 1 Coolant Hydradrive!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.340
After Wind comes Water.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:15.650
The Continuous Trap, Hydradrive 
Generator’s effect activates!

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:19.220
I Special Summon Hydradrive 
Token in defense position!

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:24.490
Appear again!  The circuit 
that connects the truth!

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:28.210
The summoning condition is one Hydradrive!

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:29.770
Link Summon!

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:33.330
Link 1 Coolant Hydradrive!

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:38.060
The Continuous Trap, 
Property Spray’s effect!

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:42.170
I tribute the Water monster, 
Coolant Hydradrive!

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:49.920
I gain LP equal to its ATK, and your 
monsters change to Water Attribute!

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.920
The other Coolant Hydradrive’s effect!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:56.450
When there’s a Water Attribute 
monster on your field...

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:59.460
...this monster can attack you directly!

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:02.870
Go, Coolant Hydradrive!

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:05.100
This is…

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:09.340
The Link Spell, Judgment Arrows’ effect.

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:16.210
When the Link Monster linked to 
this card battles, its ATK double!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.460
It’s the same pattern as before!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.080
If you take this, it’s over Playmaker!

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.300
Cyberse Magician’s effect!

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:28.040
The battle or effect damage I take is halved!

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.530
Cyberse Architect!

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:41.270
When I deal you battle damage...

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:46.410
...I Special Summon Covered Hydradrive 
from my hand using its own effect!

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.370
Covered Hydradrive can’t 
be destroyed in battle.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:57.120
And when there’s another Hydradrive on 
the field, I don’t take battle damage.

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:04.590
But at the beginning of my turn, all 
Hydradrive Link Monsters on my field are destroyed!

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:06.840
That’s a problem.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:12.220
If we don’t destroy those two monsters, 
our attacks won’t get through.

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:13.810
I end my turn!

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:18.780
Cyberse Magician and Cyberse Witch’s 
Attributes return to normal.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:22.560
I thought it'd be an easy win, 
but he’s fighting well.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:25.700
And he said that he wants 
to regain his memories.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.750
Something’s up with him.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:31.820
Whatever the reason, what 
he did was inexcusable.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:42.070
Yusaku, I’m counting on you.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.950
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:52.270
I discard one card to activate 
Covered Hydradrive’s effect!

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:57.360
You can only attack with 
one monster this turn!

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:02.320
Playmaker, we can only 
attack with one monster!

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:03.960
How'll we get through?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.640
Ai, let's do that thing!

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:08.690
I was waiting for you to say that!

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.760
Let’s go!

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:17.660
Come, Data Storm!

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:26.810
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:32.000
That’s…

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:35.160
I activate my Skill!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:43.090
When I have 1000 or fewer LP, I can add a 
random monster in the Data Storm to my Extra Deck!

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:46.890
Storm Access!

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.940
I'll end it this turn!

00:15:55.510 --> 00:16:01.110
I banish two Cyberses from my 
graveyard - Elphase and Dotscaper!

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:04.770
I Special Summon Degrade Buster from my hand!

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:10.050
Dotscaper’s effect activates!

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:15.020
When this card is banished, 
it can Special Summon itself!

00:16:15.520 --> 00:16:18.520
When Linkuriboh is in my graveyard...

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.000
...I can tribute a Level 1 
monster to activate its effect!

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:24.400
I tribute Dotscaper!

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.400
Resurrect, Linkuriboh!

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.990
Then I activate my trap, Break & Reverse!

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.600
It destroys a Link Monster...

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:42.020
...and Special Summons a monster with equal or 
fewer ATK from my graveyard by negating its effects.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.820
I destroy Linkuriboh with 300 ATK!

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:49.530
Resurrect, Defcon Bird!

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:53.390
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:59.380
I set Degrade Buster and Defcon 
Bird in the Link Markers!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.420
Link Summon!

00:17:02.420 --> 00:17:05.710
Link 2 Recovery Sorcerer!

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:10.040
Recovery Sorcerer’s effect activates.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:15.790
I Special Summon a monster in my 
graveyard that was destroyed this turn.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:18.780
Resurrect again, Linkuriboh!

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:22.530
Good!  Everything's ready!

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:25.990
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.470
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:34.000
I set Linkuriboh and Link 2 Recovery 
Sorcerer in the Link Markers!

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.970
Link Summon!

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:43.410
Appear, Link 3 Shootingcode Talker!

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:56.940
That’s a new Code Talker!

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:59.960
Shootingcode Talker's effect activates!

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.260
In addition to its usual attack...

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:07.450
...it gains an extra attack for 
every monster next to its links!

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:09.500
There are two next to its links.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.660
So Shootingcode Talker 
can attack three times!

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.110
Three times?

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:24.550
First!  Attack Coolant Hydradrive!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.600
Since Coolant Hydradrive was destroyed...

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:34.400
...I Special Summon a Hydradrive 
Token in defense position!

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:40.130
And due to Covered Hydradrive’s 
effect, I take 0 damage!

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:44.140
Second!  Attack Hydradrive Token!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.200
This is bad!

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:51.580
Covered Hydradrive’s effect is gone!

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:55.820
Third!  Attack Covered Hydradrive!

00:18:55.820 --> 00:19:01.000
During the turn Shootingcode Talker 
uses its effect to gain attacks...

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:07.800
...when there’s only one monster on 
your field, Shootingcode loses 400 ATK.

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:10.800
1900 damage!  No problem!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.780
Finish him, Shootingcode Talker!

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:17.500
Shooting Complete!

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:27.630
He’s tough!

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:41.370
Now give back what you stole.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.280
It's my turn, Playmaker.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:48.160
I’ll eat your memory data!

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.390
Thanks for the meal!

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.570
Ai!  What’s wrong?

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.490
Is it a virus?

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:08.780
An ally?

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:12.790
Brother, hang in there!

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:19.170
It’s a good thing I included 
an anti-Ignis program.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:22.900
Come, Bit and Boot!

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:33.800
Oh my.  The opponent is Playmaker.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:35.650
Kill two birds with one stone.

00:20:35.650 --> 00:20:38.210
Let’s retrieve the Ignis.

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.780
Let’s go, Boot.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.850
Understood, Bit.

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:44.220
Duel Mode.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:47.090
Hand over the Ignis, Playmaker.

00:20:47.390 --> 00:20:50.910
Outta the way!  I have no time for you!

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:16.020
I’ll handle them.

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:18.990
Playmaker, you go after him.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:24.990
You’re...

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:29.630
Hurry!

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:31.220
Thanks.

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.500
Let’s do this, Flame.

